  "message.googology.guide": "§bGuogaology§r\nRing: twelve blocks in a 5×5 frame without corners, empty 3×3 center.\nOverworld: whole cakes (Guogao blocks may be mixed in) + apple → Outer Googology.\nOuter: local frame + Ω material → Inner Googology.\nInner: local frame + Guogao block → Guogao Underworld.\nReturn: build a ring from local common blocks and throw in one more local block to go up one layer. Outer: dirt/planks; Inner: Number Stones/biome ground; Underworld: Guogao earth/rock/Dread Wood.\nHorizontal scales, Overworld:Outer:Inner:Underworld = 1:1:4:16.\nFalling into the Inner void leads to the Underworld at Y=500; quarter gravity and no fall damage.\nAdmin: /googology visit, inner, guogao, return.",
